This repository holds the website https://trubotshow.com. Its files are public
only because a website has to be sent to the people who visit it. It is not open
source, and no license is granted to anyone.


WHAT BELONGS TO TRUBOTSHOW

- Trubot™, the character: a ball-shaped robot with a face of LED dots. Its look,
  the arrangement and behaviour of its dots, its expressions, the way it moves,
  and every animation, scene and picture made with it.
- Trubotshow™, the name and the studio's identity.
- Everything else here that Trubotshow made: the design of the site, its code
  (including the code that draws and animates Trubot, the LED dot wall and the
  objects around it), its text, images and sounds.
- The apps Trubotshow publishes, with their names, icons and artwork.

Trubot and Trubotshow are trademarks of Trubotshow.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

- Visit the site, and read these files in your browser or on GitHub.
- Link to the site.


WHAT NEEDS WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM TRUBOTSHOW FIRST

- Copying, republishing, modifying, selling or sublicensing any part of the above.
- Using the Trubot character, or one that could be mistaken for it, in a product,
  a site, a video, merchandise or an advertisement.
- Reusing the code, in whole or in part, in another project.


